/*
  English purpose strings for the packaged Info.plist.

  iOS shows the value from the .lproj matching the device language and falls
  back to Runner/Info.plist when none matches. This English value is identical
  to the one in Runner/Info.plist, so the fallback and the localization cannot
  say different things.

  The sentence is bound by what the lock actually is. Face ID here is a LOCAL
  privacy control: the device performs the comparison and answers yes or no,
  Karar receives no template, image or derived representation, stores none and
  transmits none, and unlocking proves presence to the device rather than
  granting a session. Every clause below carries one of those facts. Shortening
  it means dropping one of them, which is why it is this long and no longer.
*/
"NSFaceIDUsageDescription" = "Face ID unlocks Karar on this device. Your device performs the check and Karar never receives or stores your face data. Unlocking the app does not replace signing in.";
